    {
      "title": "Imran Khan moves Bombay HC against notice to leave India by October 28",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/imran-khan-moves-bombay-hc-against-notice-to-leave-india-by-october-28-126101700849_1.html",
      "description": "Bollywood actor Imran Khan, a US citizen, on Saturday filed a petition in the Bombay High Court challenging a notice issued by police directing him to leave India by October 28 after he participated in a political protest, even as he received a show-cause notice from the FRRO as to why his Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) status should not be cancelled.\nThe 43-year-old actor, who had participated in a recent demonstration in Mumbai related to the agitation seeking Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation, received a show-cause notice from the Foreigners Registration Office (FRRO), said his lawyer Zulfiquar Memon.\nThis notice should have been issued before Mumbai Police issued their \"abrupt and arbitrary\" 'Leave India Notice' to Khan, the lawyer said.\nIn his plea before the High Court, the actor said the notice issued by the Mumbai police was \"illegal, arbitrary, perverse and drastic\".\nThe petition, filed through advocate Memon and MZM Legal, said the police notice ...",
